# Input
```astro
<!-- should generate diagnostics -->
<div class:list={"card active"}></div>
<div class:list={['one two', "three four"]}></div>

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.astro:2:18 lint/nursery/useAstroSplitClassList  FIXABLE  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  i Split this string into separate class:list entries.
  
    1 │ <!-- should generate diagnostics -->
  > 2 │ <div class:list={"card active"}></div>
      │                  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    3 │ <div class:list={['one two', "three four"]}></div>
    4 │ 
  
  i The string card active combines classes that Astro can represent as distinct list entries.
  
  i Replace the string with an array containing one entry for each class.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  
  i Safe fix: Split the class string into separate entries.
  
    1 │ ["card",·"active"]
      │ +     ++ +       +

```

